[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: web_server_0
diagnosis_text:
The network/OSPF core path is healthy. From host_1_1_1_1 we can reach the server subnet and web_server_0 by IP and DNS: ICMP to 10.200.0.3 (web0.local) succeeds, and other web servers (e.g., 10.200.0.4) load normally. The failure is at the application layer on web_server_0: there is no HTTP listener on TCP/80. On web_server_0, ss/netstat shows only 127.0.0.11 listening (container DNS), with no socket on 0.0.0.0:80. systemctl reports apache2.service is loaded but inactive (dead). From the client, a direct TCP test to 10.200.0.3:80 fails immediately (nc exit 1), and curl to http://web0.local yields no starttransfer (no response body), while curl to other servers completes, confirming the path is fine but the service is down. iptables on web_server_0 is wide open (default ACCEPT), so this is not a firewall drop.

Affected component: Apache HTTP daemon on web_server_0 (application/service layer).
Mechanism: With no process bound to TCP/80, SYNs are refused/timeout, so the browser “spins” and never loads content.
Localization: web_server_0, HTTP service (apache2), interface eth0 (IP 10.200.0.3).
Root cause: The Apache service on web_server_0 is stopped (inactive), leaving no HTTP listener on port 80.
Corrective fix: Restart the web service on web_server_0: systemctl restart apache2 (and verify ss -ltn shows 0.0.0.0:80). No router/switch or OSPF changes are required.
=== END ===